.TH BACAK-DM-SETUP 1 "June 2026" "BDM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bacak-dm-setup \- install, enable, revert and uninstall the Bacak Display Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacak-dm-setup
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bacak-dm-setup
manages making the Bacak Display Manager (BDM) the system display manager, with
a built-in recovery path. Run as root.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Ensure runtime dependencies (weston, dbus), install the real
.BR bacak-compositor (1)
if resolvable, and the
.B bacak-session
wrapper. Does NOT change the active display manager.
.TP
.B enable
Make BDM the display manager, disabling the current one. Prints recovery
instructions and asks to confirm. By default it takes effect on the next reboot.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-autologin \fIUSER\fR
Also enable autologin for \fIUSER\fR (the most-verified mode).
.TP
.B \-\-now
Switch immediately instead of on reboot (ends the current graphical session).
.TP
.B \-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.RE
.TP
.B revert
Recovery: re-enable and start the previous display manager. Run from a text
console (Ctrl+Alt+F3) if the graphical login does not appear.
.TP
.B status
Show what is installed and which display manager is active.
.TP
.B uninstall
Revert to the previous display manager, then remove the BDM package.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BDM_COMPOSITOR
Path to a prebuilt
.B bacak-compositor
binary to install.
.TP
.B BDM_COMPOSITOR_SRC
Path to the compositor source workspace (built if no binary is found).
.TP
.B BDM_DEB
Path to the BDM .deb (used by
.B install
when run from a source tree).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bacak-display-manager (8),
.BR bacak-compositor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Bacak Desktop Project.
